common --enable_bzlmod

# ── Local execution only (NO BuildBuddy / RBE) ───────────────────────────────
# haku-state deliberately runs everything locally: it may hold private operator
# info, so its source never leaves the cluster's own Forgejo Actions runner.
# There is no --remote_executor / --remote_cache. An on-disk cache keeps rebuilds
# fast, but --disk_cache is a machine-specific path so it lives in each user's /
# the CI runner's ~/.bazelrc (a standard home bazelrc Bazel reads automatically),
# not here — see tools/ci/trust_egress_ca.sh for the runner's.
build --spawn_strategy=local

# TODO(devinfra-session-tooling): devinfra/claude/claude_hook/main.rs's session bazelrc
#   writer unconditionally emits `build --config=rbe` (in buildbuddy.bazelrc) and
#   `common --config=ai_agent`, assuming every repo a Claude Code session touches is
#   ducktape. Fix that assumption there (e.g. only emit configs the target repo actually
#   defines, or make them genuinely repo-agnostic) so non-ducktape repos like this one
#   don't need matching no-op shims at all. Until then, define both here as no-ops —
#   genuinely no remote executor is wired below, so this stays exactly as local as the
#   rest of this file — purely so the flag resolves instead of erroring "Config value
#   'rbe' is not defined" in an agent session.
build:rbe --spawn_strategy=local

# Strict action env: actions get a fixed PATH instead of inheriting the client's
# PATH. Keeps builds reproducible across the runner and dev machines.
build --incompatible_strict_action_env

# Don't generate empty __init__.py stubs in runfiles (namespace-package hygiene).
common --incompatible_default_to_explicit_init_py

# Use the shell bootstrap so py_binary invokes the hermetic interpreter directly
# rather than `#!/usr/bin/env python3` (avoids _sre.MAGIC mismatch / stdlib
# shadowing when a system python differs from the 3.13 toolchain).
common --@rules_python//python/config_settings:bootstrap_impl=script

# Pin the Python version so mixed toolchains never leak in.
build --@rules_python//python/config_settings:python_version=3.13

# Quiet, non-interactive output for CI logs.
common:ci --curses=no
common:ci --show_progress_rate_limit=30

# Same devinfra tooling gap as the `rbe` no-op above (see the TODO there) — the session
# bazelrc unconditionally sets `common --config=ai_agent` too. Define it here to match
# ducktape's own `ai_agent` config until the tooling stops assuming every repo is ducktape.
common:ai_agent --curses=no
common:ai_agent --show_progress_rate_limit=30
common:ci --announce_rc
# Print failing test logs inline (they're otherwise only in bazel-testlogs, which
# CI doesn't upload) so a failure is diagnosable from the run output.
test:ci --test_output=errors

# ── Egress: proxy + CA for the in-cluster CI runner ──────────────────────────
# The haku-ci runner reaches bcr.bazel.build / GitHub / nodejs.org / npm / PyPI
# through haku-egress-proxy (a TLS-bumping forward proxy). Two needs, neither in
# this checked-in .bazelrc so a local `bazel build` (direct egress) is unaffected:
#
#  - Proxy routing: the runner injects HTTP(S)_PROXY / NO_PROXY into the job
#    container env (cluster/k8s/haku-ci/config.yaml). Bazel's repository
#    downloader honors the http_proxy/https_proxy env vars, so no flag is needed.
#  - CA trust: the proxy bumps TLS with the cluster's egress CA. Bazel's
#    downloader runs in the server JVM, which validates against a Java KeyStore —
#    NOT SSL_CERT_FILE/CURL_CA_BUNDLE (those cover curl/python/node). The CI job
#    imports the CA into the distro Java truststore and points the server JVM at
#    it via the runner's ~/.bazelrc (Bazel reads the home bazelrc automatically,
#    so no checked-in try-import is needed and local/CLI builds are unaffected) —
#    see .forgejo/workflows/bazel-ci.yaml ("Trust egress-proxy CA") and
#    tools/ci/trust_egress_ca.sh.
#
# TODO(egress-transparency): make CA trust less bespoke than a per-run keytool
#   import into ~/.bazelrc — e.g. JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS from the runner env, or bake
#   the CA into the job image / point Bazel at a system JDK whose cacerts
#   ca-certificates-java already syncs. (operator, this session)
